  "lineage": "Music of the Mande skin-faced spike lute of Mali and Guinea, the jeli ngoni of the Kouyaté and Sissoko lineages and the hunters' donso ngoni of Wassoulou, documented since the fourteenth-century Mali empire and brought to modern prominence by Banzoumana Sissoko, Moriba Koïta and Bassekou Kouyaté — four to seven strings plucked with a dry percussive attack, cyclic pentatonic ostinati at 90-130 BPM, buzzing metal jangler resonance, and interlocking with a second ngoni and calabash percussion under praise or hunters' song.",
